THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

FlowClip's own source code is MIT licensed as above. The Windows installer also
redistributes the following, which carry their own terms:

FFmpeg (ffmpeg.exe, ffprobe.exe)
  Licence : GNU General Public License v3 or later
  Build   : https://github.com/BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds  (win64-gpl)
  Source  : https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg
  Licence text: https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.html

  FlowClip invokes FFmpeg as a separate executable and contains no FFmpeg code,
  so the two remain separate works. The GPL build is used because H.264 export
  depends on libx264, which is not present in LGPL builds. The complete
  corresponding source for the bundled binaries is available at the FFmpeg
  repository above, and the exact build scripts at the BtbN repository.

Electron, React and the other npm dependencies are distributed under their own
licences; see the respective packages for details.
